.com/photo/msid-132763233,imgsize-267821.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[World's first power plant: Salt water meets fresh water to generate electricity]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132760943.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/the-netherlands-built-the-worlds-first-power-plant-where-salt-water-meets-fresh-water-to-generate-electricity-hidden-inside-a-small-blue-building/articleshow/132760943.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/the-netherlands-built-the-worlds-first-power-plant-where-salt-water-meets-fresh-water-to-generate-electricity-hidden-inside-a-small-blue-building/articleshow/132760943.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-07-31T15:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132761091,imgsize-140922.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[U.S. avocado imports cut chemical use, reduce nitrogen pollution by 10%]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132758920.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[New United States import rules for Mexican avocados prompted growers to reduce chemical use. This change significantly lowered nitrogen pollution in nearby Mexican waterways. Stricter inspections and phytosanitary certificates encouraged more careful pest management practices. The market access incentivized cleaner production methods without halting trade. This demonstrates how trade policies can yield unexpected environmental benefits.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/america-allowed-avocados-from-across-mexico-under-stricter-inspection-rules-in-2016-farmers-reduced-routine-chemical-use-and-nearby-nitrogen-pollution-fell-about-10/articleshow/132758920.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/america-allowed-avocados-from-across-mexico-under-stricter-inspection-rules-in-2016-farmers-reduced-routine-chemical-use-and-nearby-nitrogen-pollution-fell-about-10/articleshow/132758920.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-07-31T15:10:10+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132759134,imgsize-154376.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[14-year-old Montana boy uses Rodeo Lasso to save drowning man on camping trip]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132761633.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A family camping trip in Montana turned into a dramatic rescue when 14-year-old Jory Thomas used his rodeo lasso skills to save a man from the fast-moving Yellowstone River. After a raft and paddleboard crashed into a bridge pillar, one person was swept downstream. Jory roped the man on his first attempt and pulled him safely to shore before emergency responders arrived.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-14-year-old-montana-boy-brought-his-rodeo-lasso-on-a-family-camping-trip-hours-later-he-used-it-to-save-a-drowning-man/articleshow/132761633.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-14-year-old-montana-boy-brought-his-rodeo-lasso-on-a-family-camping-trip-hours-later-he-used-it-to-save-a-drowning-man/articleshow/132761633.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-07-31T15:13:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132762613,imgsize-51222.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Solved water crisis by turning seawater into drinking water using solar power]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132759243.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/how-a-tiny-south-african-fishing-village-solved-its-water-crisis-by-turning-seawater-into-drinking-water-using-solar-power/articleshow/132759243.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/how-a-tiny-south-african-fishing-village-solved-its-water-crisis-by-turning-seawater-into-drinking-water-using-solar-power/articleshow/132759243.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-07-31T14:30:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132760543,imgsize-2001139.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Scientists trained 182 pet dogs to sniff out one of America's most destructive invasive insects, and most successfully found its hidden eggs]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132762772.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/scientists-trained-182-pet-dogs-to-sniff-out-one-of-americas-most-destructive-invasive-insects-and-most-successfully-found-its-hidden-eggs/articleshow/132762772.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/scientists-trained-182-pet-dogs-to-sniff-out-one-of-americas-most-destructive-invasive-insects-and-most-successfully-found-its-hidden-eggs/articleshow/132762772.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-07-31T15:15:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132762842,imgsize-1266235.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Archaeologists discovered Spain's oldest known Roman library inside a villa in Córdoba]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132762002.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Archaeologists identified a room at Fuente Álamo as the oldest Roman library.  This space was previously thought to be a shrine to the god Mithras.  The library's architecture matches known Roman library designs and is the westernmost in the empire.  Its discovery highlights the cultural ambitions of its wealthy owner.  This finding offers a unique glimpse into Roman intellectual life in Baetica.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/archaeologists-discovered-spains-oldest-known-roman-library-inside-a-villa-in-crdoba/articleshow/132762002.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/archaeologists-discovered-spains-oldest-known-roman-library-inside-a-villa-in-crdoba/articleshow/132762002.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-07-31T15:15:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132762053,imgsize-77133.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[In 2003, a retired man planted trees on forgotten land alone; 20 years later, it had become one of Sao Paulo's largest urban forests]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132761848.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/in-2003-a-retired-man-planted-trees-on-forgotten-land-alone-20-years-later-it-had-become-one-of-sao-paulos-largest-urban-forests/articleshow/132761848.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/in-2003-a-retired-man-planted-trees-on-forgotten-land-alone-20-years-later-it-had-become-one-of-sao-paulos-largest-urban-forests/articleshow/132761848.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-07-31T14:17:33+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132762031,imgsize-280949.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Teen lifeguard saves 3 in massive waves on first day, earns Trump’s praise]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132733414.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A 16-year-old lifeguard named Ryder Williams performed a dramatic ocean rescue in Santa Cruz. He bravely pulled a 10-year-old boy from powerful surf at Seabright Beach. After his shift, Williams also helped save two more individuals in a separate incident. This heroic teenager received nationwide praise for his actions and bravery. His dedication highlights the importance of lifeguard training and quick response.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/california-rookie-lifeguard-ryder-williams-saved-a-10-year-old-from-10-foot-waves-in-his-first-rescue-after-his-shift-the-16-year-old-helped-save-two-more-people-and-won-trumps-praise/articleshow/132733414.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/california-rookie-lifeguard-ryder-williams-saved-a-10-year-old-from-10-foot-waves-in-his-first-rescue-after-his-shift-the-16-year-old-helped-save-two-more-people-and-won-trumps-praise/articleshow/132733414.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-07-31T14:00:43+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132733470,imgsize-46807.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[14-year-old Indian American girl builds system to predict driver fatigue, eyes $25,000 prize]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132759565.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Fourteen-year-old Indian-American student Sharvi Mahajan has developed NeuroDrive Alert, an EEG-based machine learning system that tracks brain activity to predict driver fatigue before microsleep occurs. Her innovation has earned her a place among the 10 finalists of the 2026 3M Young Scientist Challenge, where she will compete for a $25,000 prize.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/san-diego-student-sharvi-mahajan-14-designed-an-eeg-based-ai-system-to-predict-driver-fatigue-and-microsleep-she-is-now-competing-for-a-25000-science-prize/articleshow/132759565.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/san-diego-student-sharvi-mahajan-14-designed-an-eeg-based-ai-system-to-predict-driver-fatigue-and-microsleep-she-is-now-competing-for-a-25000-science-prize/articleshow/132759565.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-07-31T13:30:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132760316,imgsize-84947.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[America cancelled the world's most powerful particle collider, leaving a 22.5-km tunnel hidden beneath Texas for more than 30 years]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132761201.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/america-cancelled-the-worlds-most-powerful-particle-collider-leaving-a-22-5-km-tunnel-hidden-beneath-texas-for-more-than-30-years/articleshow/132761201.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/america-cancelled-the-worlds-most-powerful-particle-collider-leaving-a-22-5-km-tunnel-hidden-beneath-texas-for-more-than-30-years/articleshow/132761201.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-07-31T13:58:33+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132761590,imgsize-186972.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[ 400 hours counting caterpillars changed what we knew about LED lighting]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132760941.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/a-phd-student-spent-400-hours-counting-caterpillars-under-streetlights-his-findings-changed-what-scientists-knew-about-led-lighting/articleshow/132760941.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/a-phd-student-spent-400-hours-counting-caterpillars-under-streetlights-his-findings-changed-what-scientists-knew-about-led-lighting/articleshow/132760941.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-07-31T13:51:06+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132761165,imgsize-64732.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Australia's mysterious 'Birdman' has spent two years feeding birds in the middle of the night, leaving the neighbourhood plagued by a daily 'poo explosion']]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132759862.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/australias-mysterious-birdman-has-spent-two-years-feeding-birds-in-the-middle-of-the-night-leaving-the-neighbourhood-plagued-by-a-daily-poo-explosion/articleshow/132759862.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/australias-mysterious-birdman-has-spent-two-years-feeding-birds-in-the-middle-of-the-night-leaving-the-neighbourhood-plagued-by-a-daily-poo-explosion/articleshow/132759862.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-07-31T13:02:27+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132760110,imgsize-1189325.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Texas engineers are building fish-like nano-robots that could harvest lithium from seawater and transform the future of clean energy]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132758439.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Texas A&amp;M engineers are developing fish-like nano-robots to harvest lithium from seawater.  These autonomous microscopic robots use specialised particles activated by light for movement.  This innovative approach offers a sustainable alternative to traditional land-based mining methods.  ]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/texas-engineers-are-building-fish-like-nano-robots-that-could-harvest-lithium-from-seawater-and-transform-the-future-of-clean-energy/articleshow/132758439.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/texas-engineers-are-building-fish-like-nano-robots-that-could-harvest-lithium-from-seawater-and-transform-the-future-of-clean-energy/articleshow/132758439.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-07-31T12:34:11+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132758814,imgsize-170259.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[US Summer heat leaves multiple hikers dehydrated in New York's Adirondacks]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132758020.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[New York Forest Rangers responded to a series of rescues across the Adirondacks in June, helping dehydrated hikers, treating medical emergencies, locating lost visitors and tackling a wildfire. Several incidents were linked to hot weather, prompting officials to remind people to carry enough water, prepare properly and follow hiking safety guidelines.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/us-summer-heat-triggered-multiple-dehydration-emergencies-in-new-yorks-adirondacks-where-hikers-needed-airlifts-iv-fluids-and-overnight-rescues/articleshow/132758020.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/us-summer-heat-triggered-multiple-dehydration-emergencies-in-new-yorks-adirondacks-where-hikers-needed-airlifts-iv-fluids-and-overnight-rescues/articleshow/132758020.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-07-31T12:32:26+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132759280,imgsize-189499.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[34 killed as methane explosion tears through coal mine in Pakistan's Balochistan]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132758457.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A methane gas explosion in Pakistan's Balochistan province killed at least thirty-four miners. Ten miners remained trapped underground after the blast ripped through the coal mine. Rescue teams worked against time to locate and recover the remaining trapped workers. Authorities announced compensation for the families of the deceased miners. The incident highlights ongoing safety concerns within Pakistan's coal mining industry.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/pakistan/34-killed-as-methane-explosion-tears-through-coal-mine-in-pakistans-balochistan/articleshow/132758457.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/pakistan/34-killed-as-methane-explosion-tears-through-coal-mine-in-pakistans-balochistan/articleshow/132758457.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-07-31T12:25:03+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Abhishek Mishra</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132758616,imgsize-1750713.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[After decades of drought, water is returning to the south of Sahara Desert as ancient farming techniques and the Great Green Wall breathe new life into the Sahel]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132757460.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/after-decades-of-drought-water-is-returning-to-the-south-of-the-sahara-desert-as-ancient-farming-techniques-and-the-great-green-wall-breathe-new-life-into-the-sahel/articleshow/132757460.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/after-decades-of-drought-water-is-returning-to-the-south-of-the-sahara-desert-as-ancient-farming-techniques-and-the-great-green-wall-breathe-new-life-into-the-sahel/articleshow/132757460.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-07-31T11:29:07+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132757762,imgsize-1878883.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[The Southern Ocean may be Earth’s safest place to remove carbon from the atmosphere, scientists find]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132758341.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/the-southern-ocean-may-be-earths-safest-place-to-remove-carbon-from-the-atmosphere-scientists-find/articleshow/132758341.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/the-southern-ocean-may-be-earths-safest-place-to-remove-carbon-from-the-atmosphere-scientists-find/articleshow/132758341.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-07-31T12:06:07+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132758456,imgsize-105060.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[German proverb of the day: "A fence lasts 3 years, a dog lasts 3 fences, a horse lasts 3 dogs, and a man lasts…"]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132755209.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[An old German proverb highlights life's transient nature and the importance of valuing time.  It uses symbolic lifespans to show everything has a limited existence.  This message remains relevant as daily life continues to change rapidly.  The proverb encourages appreciating ordinary moments and relationships over possessions.  It reminds us that life's meaning comes from how years are spent, not just their length.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/german-proverb-of-the-day-a-fence-lasts-3-years-a-dog-lasts-3-fences-a-horse-lasts-3-dogs-and-a-man-lasts-a-timeless-lesson-on-lifes-seasons-and-the-value-of-time/articleshow/132755209.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/german-proverb-of-the-day-a-fence-lasts-3-years-a-dog-lasts-3-fences-a-horse-lasts-3-dogs-and-a-man-lasts-a-timeless-lesson-on-lifes-seasons-and-the-value-of-time/articleshow/132755209.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-07-31T11:04:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132757312,imgsize-286190.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Tiny reef fish thrived near seabird islands; where rats wiped birds out, marine food chains changed]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132756134.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Tropical islands are facing a surprising ecological shift as invasive rats disrupt the balance of coral reef ecosystems. By decimating seabird numbers, these rats cut down on essential nutrient contributions to the reefs. As a result, tiny cryptobenthic fish flourish in nutrient-rich spots, while invertebrates find success in less fertile regions, reshaping the food web and highlighting the vulnerable nature of these priceless underwater habitats.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/tiny-reef-fish-flourished-beside-islands-filled-with-seabirds-where-rats-removed-the-birds-the-entire-underwater-food-chain-took-another-route/articleshow/132756134.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/tiny-reef-fish-flourished-beside-islands-filled-with-seabirds-where-rats-removed-the-birds-the-entire-underwater-food-chain-took-another-route/articleshow/132756134.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-07-31T10:22:37+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132756229,imgsize-122197.cms"/></item></channel></rss>